# DATA class (see .dataclass.json): real-run output and real config. It lives in a config root in the
# PRIVATE companion (CONFIG.md; found by guards/tools/datadir.py or selected with
# SHOPPING_AGGREGATOR_CONFIG) and is PHYSICALLY ABSENT from this repo. The repo ships only generated
# `.example` schemas, so a fresh clone is a usable, uninitialized tool with nothing real inside it.
#
# live-runs.jsonl is why this section exists. It is append-only telemetry of REAL runs — one line per
# source touched — so it accumulated which products were priced, which retailers were bought from and
# which region they ship to. Every content scan passed it: there is no email or phone in a domain
# slug. The leak was never a bad regex, it was a pipe pointing at a public repo.
skills/shopping-aggregator/metrics/live-runs.jsonl
skills/shopping-aggregator/metrics/gh-api-cache.json
!skills/shopping-aggregator/metrics/*.example

# A config root's files, if one were ever created or copied in here. CONFIG.md, Storage.
/profile.json
/registry.json
/people/
/data/
/reference/
/row.json
# The same names one level down are refused by verify_matrix (CONFIGROOT); ignoring them here keeps
# a copied root out of a plain `git add`.
profile.json
purchases.jsonl
skills/shopping-aggregator/config/profile.json
skills/shopping-aggregator/config/registry.json
skills/shopping-aggregator/config/purchases.jsonl
skills/shopping-aggregator/config/forwarder-table.json

# Evaluation DATA belongs only in the versioned PRIVATE companion.
evaluation/
skills/shopping-aggregator/evaluation/
skills/shopping-aggregator/reference/scenario-eval/.judge-prompt.*
